You are on **macOS**.  The DEFAULT shell is **zsh** (`/bin/zsh`) — write
standard Unix commands (`ls`, `cat`, `grep`, `cp`, `mv`, `rm -rf`, ...) using
syntax that is portable across zsh and bash.
File paths use forward slashes (`/`).
Pass `terminal="zsh"` (or `"bash"` / `"sh"`) when a command genuinely needs
that interpreter; they are the exception, not the default.
